
Commando's

xya
xya,b
  x: commando
  y: motor left or right (l or not-l)
       if not used: m (don't care), normally use commandletter, e.g. pp0,0
  a: par1
  b: par2
     a and b : integer

i        :    info, prints:
	        PApp: bat, encoder1, encoder2, gearvalue
		 bat: battery voltage or >= 100 to indicate error.
                      When >= 100 reset device
mmx,y    :    set setpoints (small steps)
pmx,y    :    set setpoints  (-5, ..  + 5)
                one step = gearvalue
syx      :    set motor speed of a motor
e        :    print corrections, eepromcnt, stepsdone
f        :    print PID values and battery value
g        :    print serialnumber, version, gearvalue, max command time
Gmg      :    set gearvalue g
X        :    init eeprom data  (after that, set accuval correct again)
Y        :    zero encoders (also use F to save to permanent memory)
E        :    print error, save data in eeprom
F        :    save data in eeprom
Sms      :    set serial number and passkey
Z        :    print data collected after command p
Pmx,y    :    set P values
Imx,y    :    set I values
Dmx,y    :    set D values
Ayx      :    (L) set accuval, (R) get accuval   (Commando F niet vergeten)
Tmx      :    test motors. move motor randomly x times, end on position 0,0
C        :    Calibrate motors: go to end stop and then to new position 0,0

## testing
ty       :    start (L) of stop (R) timer
qy       :    start (L) if stop (R) motor/encoder
cy       :    control on (L) and off (R)
